"في تقرير الميكانيكي يسأل المشرف بالمضارع التام (<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Have you checked the tyres yet?</span>)، لأنه يهمه أن العمل انتهى الآن. ويجيب الميكانيكي بالماضي البسيط (<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes, we checked all the tyres first thing this morning.</span>)، لأنه يذكر <b>وقتاً محدداً</b>.": "In the mechanic's report, the supervisor asks in the present perfect (<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Have you checked the tyres yet?</span>), because he cares that the work is finished now. The mechanic answers in the past simple (<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes, we checked all the tyres first thing this morning.</span>), because he mentions a <b>definite time</b>.",
